From 332f54057218b521be96156e09b42143312ec47c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrea Manica <am315@cam.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:48:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Save the alleles of the loci as codes in .gt files (4x faster
 gt_load())

Saving and loading a character vector costs a call for each element, and
loading creates or finds the CHARSXP of each element: with tens of millions
of loci, the two allele columns took two thirds of the time of saving and
loading a .gt file. save_gt_file() now replaces them (in the copy saved)
with a code per locus (raw, or integer with more than 255 distinct alleles)
into the distinct alleles, found by the address of their CHARSXP
(encode_alleles_cpp()); gt_load() turns them back into the same strings
(restore_loci_alleles(), decode_alleles_cpp()), in their columns' place.
The allele columns are removed from the saved table, so that older versions
stop with an error rather than use wrong alleles; .gt files of older
versions load as before.

Baboon data (486 individuals x 91.2M loci, names_as_int), manica01, one
P-core, -O2 installs, 3 balanced runs: gt_load() 17.21 -> 4.13 s, saving
the .gt 20.89 -> 7.25 s, file 305 -> 225 MB; the loaded loci tables are
identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
